  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Guidance is optional, may use only information visible to the relevant players, and must leave each player’s final choice with that player.\", \"decision\": \"How should inexperienced players receive strategic guidance?\", \"goal\": \"Help guests find compatible games, understand how to play, and enjoy the evening without avoidable waiting or confusion.\", \"problem\": \"A community room is hosting an evening of board games for adults with different levels of experience. Several tables, a host, willing game teachers, short waiting activities, and a varied collection are available. Guests can decline any game and join a later one. Every game has an agreed latest stopping time before the room closes, and ordinary refreshments and conversation have their own small areas.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nBefore play, each inexperienced player chooses a willing partner who can quietly discuss visible options when invited. A consistent source of help makes questions easier to ask without turning every decision into a table-wide lesson.\nInexperienced players ask the teacher for strategic guidance when they want it, and the teacher explains the visible tradeoffs. Help responds to the player’s request while preserving their control over the final move.\nAt agreed pauses, the teacher offers the whole table a brief discussion of visible strategic considerations that players may decline. Useful guidance is offered regularly without singling out the least experienced person or choosing anyone’s move."
    }
  ],
